---
config:
    theme: redux-dark-color
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Sender
    participant ClientUI
    participant MessagingAPI@{ "type": "boundary" }
    participant SessionStore@{ "type" : "database" }
    participant BlocklistStore@{ "type" : "database" }
    participant MessageStore@{ "type" : "database" }
    actor Recipient

    Note over Sender,MessageStore: Direct message scenario. Sender is User B and Recipient is User A. Sender must have an authenticated session (FR-01 to FR-04).
    Sender->>ClientUI: Send direct message to User A with body Hello
    ClientUI->>MessagingAPI: POST /api/v1/messages/direct with recipient, body, and session token
    MessagingAPI->>SessionStore: Validate session token on this request
    SessionStore-->>MessagingAPI: Session valid or invalid

    alt Session invalid or expired
        MessagingAPI-->>ClientUI: HTTP 401 or 403 Unauthorized
        ClientUI-->>Sender: Ask user to authenticate again
    else Session valid
        MessagingAPI->>BlocklistStore: Check whether User A blocked User B
        Note right of BlocklistStore: FR-13: Do not reveal the block state to User B.
        BlocklistStore-->>MessagingAPI: Block relation found or not found

        alt User A has blocked User B
            MessagingAPI-->>ClientUI: Generic delivery failure or silent drop indicator
            Note over MessagingAPI,Recipient: A blocked message is not stored or delivered. The block state is not disclosed.
            ClientUI-->>Sender: Show only a generic failure indicator if returned
        else Contact allowed
            MessagingAPI->>MessageStore: Persist message with gapless sequence, ISO-8601 UTC timestamp, and SENT status
            Note over MessageStore,Recipient: Persist before delivery acknowledgement (NFR-04). Sequence is strictly increasing (FR-16).
            MessageStore-->>MessagingAPI: Stored message ID, sequence, timestamp, and SENT status
            MessagingAPI-->>ClientUI: HTTP 200 with message ID, sequence, and SENT status
            ClientUI-->>Sender: Display Sent

            alt Recipient has an active client session
                MessagingAPI-->>Recipient: Socket push with message ID, sequence, timestamp, and body
                Recipient-->>MessagingAPI: Receive acknowledgement
                MessagingAPI->>MessageStore: Update status to DELIVERED
                MessageStore-->>MessagingAPI: DELIVERED status saved
                MessagingAPI-->>ClientUI: Telemetry update with DELIVERED status
                ClientUI-->>Sender: Display Delivered

                Recipient->>ClientUI: Open conversation and render message
                ClientUI->>MessagingAPI: Read event for message ID
                MessagingAPI->>MessageStore: Update status to READ
                MessageStore-->>MessagingAPI: READ status saved
                MessagingAPI-->>ClientUI: Telemetry update with READ status
                ClientUI-->>Sender: Display Read
            else Recipient has no active client session
                Note over MessagingAPI,MessageStore: Keep the message stored for later retrieval (FR-07). Status remains SENT until the recipient receives it.
            end
        end
    end

    Note over Sender,Recipient: AC-02 requires Sent status, then Delivered when the target receives the message, then Read when the recipient opens/renders it. For active clients, NFR-01 sets a p95 delivery target below 200 ms at up to five concurrent sessions.